## Goal
Fix `scripts/install.sh` so that the dry-run (preview) path also fails when enumerating registered Portero app copies fails. This came out of a cross-review for DEV-46 (PR #13).

## Problems
The dry-run path piped the `lsregister -dump` output into `portero lsreg-others` inside a `while` loop. If the dump or the enumeration failed, the pipeline's exit status was lost. The preview then reported success, although the normal install path did handle that failure.

## Decision
The enumeration failure now propagates in the dry run as it already does in a real install. Because the loop was fed by a pipe, its status masked the failure of `others`. The fix is meant to make a failed Launch Services query fail the preview with a non-zero exit code. That way the preview does not claim an install would succeed when it could not list the old copies to unregister.

